  "scope": "The literal64-slot predecessor executes the real padded zero test first. Its actual returned flag selects either paid empty output allocation or the real borrow and trim child calls. The returned word is exactly BinaryArithmetic.predecessor including zero saturation and removal of all high padding. The same physical execution retains the original input and source, restores the caller, and includes the terminal attempt. Its instruction budget24L+32 and allocation bound3L+4 depend only on the original padded length; no result, zero flag, borrow result or normal form is supplied. Twelve actual physical cases cover all branches and borrow chains.",
